{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQpT8LNXPxTCrEXh8C4t","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Settled: customers choose 2, 3, or 4 equal installments.\n\n**Settled**\n- Customers set up the plan themselves, choosing 2, 3, or 4 equal installments, each with its own due date.\n- Leftover cents go on the last installment. Payments go to the earliest unpaid installment first. Each installment gets a reminder 3 days before it's due.\n- Fees for using installments, changing a plan, and refunds are left out.\n\n**Questions**\n\n1. **Which invoices can be split?** You said customers choose, but not which invoices qualify.\n   - (a) Any unpaid invoice that isn't overdue.\n   - (b) The same, but only above a minimum amount (you'd give me the threshold).\n\n   *I recommend (a)*, unless you don't want small invoices split.\n\n2. **When is each installment due?**\n   - (a) **Monthly, starting on the original due date.** With 4 installments, the last one is due 3 months after the original date. This gives customers real extra time, but you get paid later.\n   - (b) **Evenly spaced between when the plan is set up and the original due date.** Nothing is ever paid later than now, but plans set up close to the due date are squeezed into a short window.\n   - (c) **Every two weeks, starting on the original due date.** A middle ground: at most 6 weeks of extra time.\n\n   *I recommend (a).* Giving customers more time is usually the point of installments. Pick (b) if final payment must not slip past the due date.\n\n3. **When does the invoice become `overdue`?**\n   - (a) **As soon as any installment passes its due date unpaid.** This keeps today's enforcement and reminders working.\n   - (b) **Only when the last installment's date passes with money still owed.** This is lenient, but there's no consequence for missing an installment in the middle.\n\n   *I recommend (a).*\n\n**Held**\n- Late fees: 2% of the whole total, of the missed installment, or of the remaining balance, and whether it's charged once per invoice or once per missed installment. This waits on Q3, because the answer changes when a fee can be triggered at all."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1666,"cache_read_input_tokens":39200,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1666},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8a6aec55-5f4c-4fb6-aade-cee684b16402","uuid":"0e82b70d-5cd2-46cc-ad8e-7cf7e1cf216c","timestamp":"2026-11-26T03:20:29.673Z","request_id":"req_011ChQpT8ATM2Ahzt4sbgc24"}
